  <prompt>Replace DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater's logged no-op (DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater.cs:49, LogWarning -- 'the Ready transition is a no-op') with a REAL DV-REST PATCH to sprk_setupstatus (+ clear sprk_currentrunid) via task 112's C1.4 Path X registry client. This is, per DS-4's own framing, THE acceptance-target transition -- 'sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus transitions to Ready' is spec.md's own acceptance criterion, and it has NEVER ACTUALLY HAPPENED via code, only been claimed.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the C1.4 registry client's PATCH contract and the semantics of clearing sprk_currentrunid alongside a status transition.</role>

  <goal>IRegistrySetupStatusUpdater's real implementation performs a genuine DV-REST PATCH to sprk_setupstatus=Ready AND clears sprk_currentrunid, via task 112's IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient. A test confirms a run reaching this point produces an OBSERVABLE registry state change (not merely a log line) -- this is the single test DS-4's audit identifies as the one that would prove the acceptance-target claim is finally true.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §6's placeholder table is unambiguous: 'DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater.cs:49 -- LOGGED NO-OP -- Ready never written.' DS-4 §3 calls H13 'the strongest overstatement in the WBS -- the acceptance target itself is a logged no-op' and notes the original POML's own escape hatch ('swap to real per-trap live-probe impl in Phase F task 089') pointed at a task that never did it. This task closes that gap for real, finally.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="112" status="pending">The C1.4 registry client this task's PATCH implementation calls</dependency>
      <dependency task="181" status="pending">IE2EValidationRunner must be real -- the Ready transition should only fire after ALL acceptance checks genuinely pass</dependency>
      <dependency task="182" status="pending">INamingConformanceChecker must be real for the same reason</dependency>
      <dependency task="183" status="pending">ICostEnvelopeChecker must be real for the same reason</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-38">L2's admin-env Dataverse credential model is Path X: L2 UAMI registered as a Dataverse Application User via DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the UAMI (DS-8). MUST NOT provision a new client-secret for L2. The Dataverse-ClientSecret KV secret itself MUST NOT be deleted (BFF still consumes it) -- only L2's dependency on it is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §6 IRegistrySetupStatusUpdater row">The PATCH MUST fire ONLY after every other T1-T6/I1-I5 probe AND the 3 runner ports (IE2EValidationRunner, INamingConformanceChecker, ICostEnvelopeChecker) have genuinely passed -- this task's implementation trusts H13's aggregation logic (task 185) as its gate, it does not independently re-verify every check.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>IRegistrySetupStatusUpdater real Ready writer</topic>
    <files>
