  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater.cs:49's no-op in full, plus IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient's PATCH contract.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Real PATCH">Implement the PATCH: sprk_setupstatus=Ready, sprk_currentrunid cleared, via the C1.4 client.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Wire up">Replace the no-op logger call site in H13's owning module with the real implementation.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Test">Author a test confirming a Cosmos-side H13-Completed outcome produces an OBSERVABLE Dataverse registry state change (real write, not a log-only assertion).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If this task lands and a live-dev smoke test shows the PATCH succeeding but sprk_currentrunid failing to clear (a partial-success outcome), STOP and escalate rather than shipping a partial fix — a stuck sprk_currentrunid would block the I5 concurrency guard's next run for that customer, a correctness regression in an already-shipped mechanism (task 059).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
