  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'LogWarning.*no-op\|LogWarning.*Ready' in the updated DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater.cs (the old no-op pattern) returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms a Completed H13 outcome produces a REAL PATCH call to the C1.4 registry client with sprk_setupstatus=Ready.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms sprk_currentrunid is cleared in the SAME transition (not a separate, potentially-missed step).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An integration seam test (post task 112's live client) against a dev canary registry row confirms the PATCH actually lands and is readable back as Ready.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the C1.4 registry client (task 112) already implements the PATCH capability this task needs; nothing new to build at the client layer. Extension -- wiring H13's Ready-transition call site onto the already-built client is the direct, minimal fix. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- DS-4 calls this THE strongest overstatement in the entire Phase G'' backlog: without this fix, EVERY OTHER TASK in this entire wave decomposition could land perfectly and sprk_setupstatus would STILL never reach Ready via code -- the project's own stated goal (FR-18/SC#5) would remain provably unmet.</notes>

